    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Hyland Keating are delighted to present this attractive parcel of land extending to approximately 0.44 hectares (1.09 acres), ideally positioned in the scenic townland of Brockra, on the boundary of Ballyfin and Mountrath.\n\nOccupying a peaceful rural setting while remaining within easy reach of local amenities, this site offers an excellent opportunity for those seeking to build a family home in one of County Laois' most desirable residential locations, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nThe property enjoys extensive frontage onto a quiet country road and is naturally screened by mature trees and established vegetation, creating a private and tranquil setting. Towards the Slieve Bloom Mountains, renowned for their spectacular scenery, walking trails, mountain biking routes and outdoor recreation opportunities.\n\nOne of the unique features of this property is its location at the meeting point of the Brockra, Ballyfin and Mountrath areas, allowing future owners to enjoy the best of both communities. Ballyfin is home to the world-famous Ballyfin Demesne, while nearby Mountrath provides a comprehensive range of everyday services, schools, shops, sporting facilities and community amenities.\n\nThe site is conveniently located within a short drive of:\n\nBallyfin Community\nMountrath Town\nPortlaoise Town Centre\nM7 Motorway\nSlieve Bloom Mountains\nBallyfin Demesne Estate\nLocal primary and secondary schools\nNumerous walking, cycling and outdoor leisure amenities\n\nThe surrounding area offers an exceptional quality of life, combining the peace and beauty of the countryside with excellent accessibility to major employment centres throughout the Midlands.\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a generously sized site in a highly regarded location with stunning rural views and excellent lifestyle amenities on its doorstep.\n\nFor Sale Subject to Planning Permission"
      },
